{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothIntegerChain","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothIntegerChain","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothAuxiliaryInt","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothContradiction"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.roth_contradiction_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.roth_contradiction_int","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothIntegerChain.lean#L103-L142","doc":"**Steps 1 → 2 → 3 → 4, with the coefficient rings agreeing throughout.**\n\nStep 1 supplies the polynomial (`exists_rothPolySet_auxiliary`), step 2 turns the approximation\nquality into a lower bound on the index at the rational point, step 3 (Roth's Lemma) caps that\nindex from above, and step 4 collides them.\n\nWhat is left over is exactly what the earlier stages isolated and nothing new: `Γ_m`'s clauses\n(`hg`), the approximation quality (`hclose`, `hT`), and the two numeric comparisons (`hlog`,\n`hgap`).  Choosing parameters that satisfy them is the remaining work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_rothPolySet_auxiliary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_rothPolySet_auxiliary","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothIntegerChain.lean#L70-L95","doc":"**Step 1's output, in the shape steps 2–4 consume.**  A polynomial in `R(a; r)` whose index at\nthe *real* point `(ψα₁,…,ψα_m)` is at least `m/2 − εm`, with `a` also serving as the height bound\nstep 2 needs.\n\nThe counting condition is discharged inside, from `finrank ℚ K < 4ε²m` — so `deg α` is not a\nhypothesis of the chain, it is a condition on how large `m` must be. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_real_of_index_field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_real_of_index_field","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothIntegerChain.lean#L54-L68","doc":"**The index transports along a real embedding.**  Step 1 proves it over `K`, step 2 consumes it\nover `ℝ`; `ψ` is what says the `α_h` are real algebraic numbers.\n\n`NumberField K` is omitted — the linter is right that nothing here uses it.  The transport is a\nfact about *any* ring map to `ℝ`; that `K` is a number field is what makes `ψ` exist, not what\nmakes the index move. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.inRothPolySet_of_real_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.inRothPolySet_of_real_bound","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothIntegerChain.lean#L38-L49","doc":"**Siegel's real bound becomes `InRothPolySet`'s integer one.**  The ceiling is forced: from\n`|coeff| ≤ X` over `ℝ` the only integer bound available is `⌈X⌉`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}